---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="What I can help with · Direct Lifestyle Medicine" active="help" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>What I can help with</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Three parts of one practice. Every member gets the first one.
        The other two come in as your health calls for them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · Prevention and lifestyle medicine -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">One</span>
        <h2>Prevention and lifestyle medicine</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The foundation of the practice and the starting point for
          everyone. We look at how you live, find what is working against
          you, and change it in an order you can manage.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps c3">
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Nutrition and metabolic health</h4>
          <p>Food, blood sugar, cholesterol, weight. Real changes to how
          you eat, not a handout.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Movement</h4>
          <p>Activity and exercise built around your body, your time, and
          what you will keep doing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Sleep</h4>
          <p>How much, how good, and what is interrupting it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Stress and emotional health</h4>
          <p>What is weighing on you and how it shows up in your body.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>People around you</h4>
          <p>Connection and relationships. They affect health as much as
          most medicines do.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Alcohol, tobacco, and other habits</h4>
          <p>Honest conversation, practical steps, no lectures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rows" style="margin-top:clamp(30px,4vw,46px)">
        <div class="row">
          <b>A full assessment first</b>
          <p>Your history, medicines, conditions, risks, and the doctors
          you already see. Then screenings and tests that are due.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>A written plan</b>
          <p>What we are working on, in what order, who does what, and
          when we check. It changes as you do.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Goals we measure</b>
          <p>Blood pressure, labs, weight, sleep, how you feel. We look
          at them together and adjust.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Medical care and treatment -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Two</span>
        <h2>Medical care and treatment</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Lifestyle medicine is how I think about your care. It is not a
          rule against using medicine. When testing or treatment is the
          right tool, I use it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Evaluation and diagnosis</b>
          <p>You bring a symptom or a worry. I work it up the way any
          doctor would.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Conditions I manage</b>
          <p>High blood pressure, diabetes and prediabetes, cholesterol,
          thyroid, obesity, acid reflux, and other conditions within my
          scope. Some conditions need a specialist leading, and I will
          tell you when yours does.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicines</b>
          <p>Started, adjusted, stopped, and monitored. Reviewed as a
          whole: what is working, what is redundant, what is interacting.
          This includes modern weight medicines where they fit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Labs and imaging</b>
          <p>I order what is needed, tell you the price first where I
          can, and explain every result.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Abnormal findings</b>
          <p>Nothing sits unexplained. If something comes back off, we
          decide together what happens next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Everyday illness</b>
          <p>Infections, rashes, stomach trouble, and injuries that do
          not need an ER, when I am available.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Care coordination -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Three</span>
        <h2>Care coordination</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Part of the membership, not an extra. Most people see more than
          one clinician, and somebody has to keep the picture together.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Working with your primary care doctor</b>
          <p>If you have one, I send a summary after your first visit
          with your permission, and keep them informed. I do not
          duplicate their work or ask you to choose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Working with specialists</b>
          <p>I talk to them, read what they send, and fold it into your
          plan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Referrals</b>
          <p>When you need a doctor I am not, you get a real referral and
          a doctor who stays involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>If I am your only doctor</b>
          <p>I provide the care I can and help you set up whatever else
          you need. You are not turned away for not having one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Following up</b>
          <p>Tests ordered, results tracked, treatment checked. Handoffs
          to other clinicians or to a higher level of care when that is
          what you need.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Common situations -->
  <section class="section" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Common situations</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards c3">
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;It&rsquo;s several things at once.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Blood pressure, weight, sleep, stress. Each one manageable,
            together overwhelming. We sort out what&rsquo;s urgent, what
            matters most, and what can wait. Then we work through it in
            order.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I don&rsquo;t have a doctor right now.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            That is fine. You can join without one. I do the preventive
            and medical care I am able to do, and help you set up
            anything else you need.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I have a doctor, but I can rarely get in.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Keep them. I fill the space between: evaluation, treatment
            within my scope, and coordination so nothing falls through.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Something came back abnormal.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            A lab result or scan you want to understand. I go through it
            with you: what it means, what to do next, and what to watch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I want my conditions closely managed.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Diabetes, blood pressure, cholesterol, thyroid. Medicines
            reviewed, complications watched for, numbers moving where we
            agreed they should.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;My health and my life are tangled together.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Stress affects sleep. Sleep affects eating. Money worry sits
            under it all, and your body keeps score. We treat what needs
            treating and work the rest one realistic step at a time. When
            a counselor or financial professional is the right tool, I
            help you find one and stay involved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · What I don't do -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What I don&rsquo;t do</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            This membership is not a promise to manage every medical
            condition you have.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Emergencies</b>
          <p>Chest pain, stroke signs, severe injury: that is 911 and the
          ER, always. Afterward, I help you make sense of what happened.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Hospital care</b>
          <p>The hospital&rsquo;s doctors run the admission. I stay
          informed and manage your care when you&rsquo;re home.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialist-led conditions, alone</b>
          <p>Some conditions need an oncologist or cardiologist leading.
          I refer well, co-manage, and keep the whole picture.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Mental health beyond my safe scope</b>
          <p>Serious psychiatric illness and addiction care beyond
          primary care get honest triage and a warm handoff.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Children</b>
          <p>Adults only (18+).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Not sure if your situation fits?</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How the membership works &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
